assertion  XSH.iswcntrl.001
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswcntrl() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class cntrl as the locale definition lists it: the
           control characters of the portable character set (null, alert,
           backspace, tab, newline, vertical tab, form feed, carriage return).
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswcntrl.002
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswcntrl() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the letters, digits, punctuation and the space.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswcntrl.003
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswcntrl(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswcntrl.004
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswcntrl.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       No one of the 128 characters is both a control character and a
           printable one: iswcntrl() and iswprint() are never both non-zero.
test       t/004-cntrl-not-print.c
